          "text": "The dominant phase indexes as orthorhombic B19-type TiNi, space group **Pmma**. Representative indexing is 010 at 18.98\u00b0, 011 at 28.32\u00b0, 020 at 38.50\u00b0, 101 at 39.13\u00b0, 002 at 42.36\u00b0, 021 at 44.16\u00b0, and 022 at 58.56\u00b0. This gives approximately \\(a=2.7305\\), \\(b=4.6740\\), \\(c=4.265\\) \u00c5.\n\nSeveral additional split peaks, particularly near 42.5\u00b0 and 45.2\u00b0, indicate a surviving monoclinic B19\u2032-like component or distortion. Thus the pattern is not adequately represented by a single ideal Pmma phase.\n\n### Primary structure: orthorhombic B19 TiNi\n\n```cif\ndata_TiNi_B19_primary\n_audit_creation_method          'Indexed from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common           'Titanium nickel, B19 orthorhombic'\n_chemical_formula_structural    'TiNi'\n_chemical_formula_sum           'Ti2 Ni2'\n_cell_formula_units_Z           2\n\n_cell_length_a                   2.7305\n_cell_length_b                   4.6740\n_cell_length_c                   4.2650\n_cell_angle_alpha                90\n_cell_angle_beta                 90\n_cell_angle_gamma                90\n_cell_volume                     54.43\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt        'P m m a'\n_space_group_IT_number           51\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nTi1 Ti 2 f 0.5000 0.2500 0.2230 1.0 0.006\nNi1 Ni 2 e 0.0000 0.2500 0.6930 1.0 0.006\n```\n\n### Surviving alternative/component: monoclinic B19\u2032 TiNi\n\nThe peak splitting is compatible with a monoclinic distortion of nearly the same cell. The metric below is approximate because its reflections overlap strongly with the primary phase.\n\n```cif\ndata_TiNi_B19prime_alternative\n_audit_creation_method          'Approximate secondary component from peak splitting'\n_chemical_name_co